parameters.description:
This field is for the "Line Quality Diagnostic" test only. It is mandatory for that test. 
  - "No Resync" - the test will run without resynchronisation; 
  - "Normal" - the test will run with resynchronisation in Normal Initialisation mode, collecting the HLOG and QLN; 
  - "Robust" - the test will run with resynchronisation in Robust Initialisation mode, collecting the HLOG and QLN and provide a longer initialisation time with less strict parameters;

(Optional) The Status of this End User: 
 - 'Active' - Can be selected for new Orders and Trouble Tickets; 
 - 'Hidden' - Not selectable but may still be in use;

(Conditional) Existing Service ID for Service Transfer. Either the entire AVC # (e.g. AVC000000000000) or the last 5 digits only (e.g 00000).

Mandatory for, and only relevant to, Service Transfer orders. 

If specified, the response will indicate the matching resource via `serviceIDMatch` fields injected into the CPI resource or NTD resource UNI Port objects.

Any issues with validating the Service ID match will be indicated via a new $.siteRestrictionError object. These issues include:

 - RJ002003 - The provided AVC does not exist: {AVC}
 - RJ002004 - The provided AVC has recently been disconnected: {AVC}
 - RJ002005 - The provided AVC exists at a different location: {AVC}
 - RJ002006 - The provided AVC has recently been disconnected at a different location: {AVC}
